      },
      {
        "heading": "Variational Feedback Loop",
        "body": "QVE wraps QEE in a Rayleigh-Ritz minimization loop. The quantum device prepares a parameterized trial state and estimates the Hamiltonian expectation; the classical optimizer then updates the state parameters. The endpoint is not only an energy estimate but also a parameter prescription for reconstructing the approximate eigenstate.",
        "grounding_claim_ids": [
          "2",
          "8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Ansatz Significance",
        "body": "The paper connects the small demonstration to chemistry by discussing unitary coupled cluster and device-defined ansatz families. The UCC argument matters because fixed excitation level gives polynomially many terms after transformation, while the device-ansatz view admits circuits tailored to available hardware and coherence depth.",
        "grounding_claim_ids": [
          "3",
          "9"
        ]
